        "title": "The Columbian Exchange - The Most Consequential Food Event in History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Columbian Exchange (Alfred Crosby's term, 1972) is the transfer of plants, animals, diseases, and people between the Americas and the Old World following 1492. For food history, it is the single largest restructuring of world cuisine in recorded time — within 200 years, every major world cuisine was transformed by ingredients that had not existed in those regions before."
